      "content": "# Killing a Hung Process on Linux\n\n## 1. Find the Process\n\n```bash\nps aux | grep <process_name>\n# or\ntop        # interactive, press 'k' to kill\nhtop       # nicer interactive alternative\n```\n\nNote the **PID** (Process ID).\n\n## 2. Kill It (escalating force)\n\n| Command | Signal | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `kill <PID>` | SIGTERM (15) | \"Please shut down politely.\" |\n| `kill -9 <PID>` | SIGKILL (9) | \"Die now.\" Kernel removes it. |\n| `kill -KILL <PID>` | SIGKILL (9) | Same as above, just readable. |\n\n**Start with SIGTERM**, wait a few seconds, and only escalate to `kill -9` if it's truly hung.\n\n```bash\nkill 1",
